                        "glosses": [
                            "To clear away an obstruction."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b9e29b9-93eb-4e6b-b9ac-0eaab431bf6c",
                                "sense_id": "68855e55-2745-3d05-b476-e9c4fc5d2db8",
                                "text": "Instead of measuring time and life in snatching at rags, let us counsel together to disobstruct the sources of riches, and organise industry, domestic labours, agricultural, manufacturing, — all the labours that produce wealth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f54c1c86-bb68-4454-be1a-fb3291e603f8",
                                "sense_id": "68855e55-2745-3d05-b476-e9c4fc5d2db8",
                                "text": "Treatment is largely supportive (nasogastric suction, antibiotics, parenteral fluids and electrolytes); saline washouts of the colon and colostomy to disobstruct the bowel are the only definitive measures to arrest this complication."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9dadd73-b97c-4405-b13a-6018bb2bf188",
                                "sense_id": "68855e55-2745-3d05-b476-e9c4fc5d2db8",
                                "text": "I hope to show that their very existence is functional: they are involved ( they were born to become involved ) in a ritual action designed to disobstruct the ascendancy to kingship of their half-brother Alfonso, rey niño, ten-year- old heir to the throne vacated by Duarte."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1df2c7fb-92f7-4ea2-bac4-06c0a6309ab8",
                                "sense_id": "68855e55-2745-3d05-b476-e9c4fc5d2db8",
                                "text": "However, only nine patients in the control group did not disobstruct spontaneously and these were compared to 52 patients in whom disobstruction was spontaneous or therapeutically achieved."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
